#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186624810 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "203c3a72-98e4-5bba-8d52-643b5a8ae662" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624804} {:answer/id #uuid "b734bbd4-ed56-5dd6-a26c-7063e1357dcf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624830}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "203c3a72-98e4-5bba-8d52-643b5a8ae662" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624804} :answer-field/id #uuid "35ab60df-3af2-58f5-9cef-c78292566527" :answer-field/key "$y=- \\frac{1}{2}x+4$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624808} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "339a46f2-957b-50bf-81f3-f48099bbef4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624807} {:answer/id #uuid "60a8e9ca-aafe-5894-9859-ede2c8e74204" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624814}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "339a46f2-957b-50bf-81f3-f48099bbef4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624807} :answer-field/id #uuid "ac7eb9ed-f763-5a49-9c82-711b69bc3254" :answer-field/key "$y=4-2x$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624824} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c19a8dd4-fec8-5e9e-a375-1d5d1177cb04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624831} {:answer/id #uuid "e144ef3a-7749-5b80-99ed-efa4e654d75d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624841}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e144ef3a-7749-5b80-99ed-efa4e654d75d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624841} :answer-field/id #uuid "e6cf20e0-1e2c-58bb-8d8a-40b535d8f986" :answer-field/key "$y+\\frac{1}{2}x=4$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624843}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4348104f-2ff2-50b3-adec-adfa89f62726" :question/problem "![](images/4f/4fac094a684d7209071c624ffe184184d34d3b3439ade505555c5ecb1cbc2a02.png)\n\nWhich of the following gives the graph of the straight line above?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's pick two distinct points on the line. For example, $A$ and $B$ with coordinates $(0,4)$ and $(2,3)$, respectively.\n\n![](images/92/92b2d2e714fce68ca3b8a38d1ba35d8b35971d3bbb2a238d7d68f48042b8aa3c.png)\n\nNow, we substitute the coordinates of both points in our equations. If both points satisfy an equation, then we can conclude that the equation represents the line in the graph. Otherwise, if any point does *not* satisfy the equation, then we can conclude that the equation does *not* represent the line in the graph.\n\n- Equation: $y=- \\frac{1}{2}x+4.$\nSubstituting the coordinates of $A(0,4)$ and $B(2,3)$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(4) &=- \\frac{1}{2}(0)+4 \\\\ 4 &=4\\,\\checkmark \\\\ (3) &=- \\frac{1}{2}(2)+4 \\\\ 3 &=3\\,\\checkmark\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $y=- \\frac{1}{2}x+4$ is an equation of the line in the graph.\n\n- Equation: $y=4-2x.$\nSubstituting the coordinates of $A(0,4)$ and $B(2,3)$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(4) &=4-2(0) \\\\ 4 &=4\\,\\checkmark \\\\ (3) &=4-2(2) \\\\ 3 &=0\\,\\times\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $y=4-2x$ is *not* an equation of the line in the graph.\n\n- Equation: $y+\\frac{1}{2}x=4.$\nSubstituting the coordinates of $A(0,4)$ and $B(2,3)$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(4)+\\frac{1}{2}(0) &=4 \\\\ 4 &=4\\,\\checkmark \\\\ (3)+\\frac{1}{2}(2) &=4 \\\\ 4 &=4\\,\\checkmark\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $y+\\frac{1}{2}x=4$ is an equation of the line in the graph.\n\nSelect $y=- \\frac{1}{2}x+4$, $y+\\frac{1}{2}x=4$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186624828 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "61947825-5d54-5e7d-86aa-4fdacf87166d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624815} {:answer/id #uuid "94eee39d-1fc4-5541-b921-57ac88c96add" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624823}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "94eee39d-1fc4-5541-b921-57ac88c96add" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624823} :answer-field/id #uuid "6a299467-705e-530a-bc23-2edf622f4969" :answer-field/key "$y-2x=-2$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624817} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "13a7de2e-de37-52b1-8e53-d8cc7e9f7b60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624802} {:answer/id #uuid "d62fbe1d-e009-5b52-8668-719abb430adc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624838}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "13a7de2e-de37-52b1-8e53-d8cc7e9f7b60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624802} :answer-field/id #uuid "d624f006-00aa-5d70-a8db-84dd45b0ec04" :answer-field/key "$y=-2+\\frac{1}{2}x$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624837} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3005dfe8-0e56-5e72-91d5-ddfd6d576f0d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624806} {:answer/id #uuid "ade68938-8e0c-5bec-b216-bed7d6ad0c2b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624825}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3005dfe8-0e56-5e72-91d5-ddfd6d576f0d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624806} :answer-field/id #uuid "d8356280-4710-526b-8d59-c96daa96c3eb" :answer-field/key "$y=\\frac{1}{2}x-2$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624839}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b254416d-e106-5d67-a907-672177ee0801" :question/problem "![](images/ef/efe35f51fa4ce8707e2ac4ce1785ece55e9191bcedbe2b22ff64b5e4510eb5c7.png)\n\nWhich of the following gives the graph of the straight line above?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's pick two distinct points on the line. For example, $A$ and $B$ with coordinates $(0,-2)$ and $(2,-1)$, respectively.\n\n![](images/ac/ace116847d9b31abeb947a1e3952dc9f6aea7224602d394d9318efc51476bc6e.png)\n\nNow, we substitute the coordinates of both points in our equations. If both points satisfy an equation, then we can conclude that the equation represents the line in the graph. Otherwise, if any point does *not* satisfy the equation, then we can conclude that the equation does *not* represent the line in the graph.\n\n- Equation: $y=\\frac{1}{2}x-2.$\nSubstituting the coordinates of $A(0,-2)$ and $B(2,-1)$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-2) &=\\frac{1}{2}(0)-2 \\\\ -2 &=-2\\,\\checkmark \\\\ (-1) &=\\frac{1}{2}(2)-2 \\\\ -1 &=-1\\,\\checkmark\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $y=\\frac{1}{2}x-2$ is an equation of the line in the graph.\n\n- Equation: $y=-2+\\frac{1}{2}x.$\nSubstituting the coordinates of $A(0,-2)$ and $B(2,-1)$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-2) &=-2+\\frac{1}{2}(0) \\\\ -2 &=-2\\,\\checkmark \\\\ (-1) &=-2+\\frac{1}{2}(2) \\\\ -1 &=-1\\,\\checkmark\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $y=-2+\\frac{1}{2}x$ is an equation of the line in the graph.\n\n- Equation: $y-2x=-2.$\nSubstituting the coordinates of $A(0,-2)$ and $B(2,-1)$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-2)-2(0) &=-2 \\\\ -2 &=-2\\,\\checkmark \\\\ (-1)-2(2) &=-2 \\\\ -5 &=-2\\,\\times\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $y-2x=-2$ is *not* an equation of the line in the graph.\n\nSelect $y=\\frac{1}{2}x-2$, $y=-2+\\frac{1}{2}x$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186624845 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "433dc4d1-a082-5006-8b88-eea429c9c826" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624809} {:answer/id #uuid "73a6fa18-cc12-592c-aa0f-ebeaef416a49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624820}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "73a6fa18-cc12-592c-aa0f-ebeaef416a49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624820} :answer-field/id #uuid "0ae03a63-2324-5f95-b1f9-4b8e3ccf92c4" :answer-field/key "$2y-\\frac{4}{3}x=2$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624800} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1270f00e-620c-53b0-82cf-ea6d2e6d169b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624801} {:answer/id #uuid "ce8f3f73-c92e-5e9c-a181-ee9fad1c30bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624835}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1270f00e-620c-53b0-82cf-ea6d2e6d169b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624801} :answer-field/id #uuid "6561f578-3b95-5931-8a50-3584ec7395a2" :answer-field/key "$y=\\frac{2}{3}x+1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624816} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "192c9b37-1a1f-5454-922a-825b07a3d549" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624803} {:answer/id #uuid "2da5b28f-17d1-541c-b3b4-b2d5655e3db2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624805}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "192c9b37-1a1f-5454-922a-825b07a3d549" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624803} :answer-field/id #uuid "f1a3a07d-44a9-5ca1-896b-b834ca0f2b29" :answer-field/key "$y=1-\\frac{2}{3}x$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624847}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e8c03d59-eacf-5f7a-bb18-0f76f1a5d12b" :question/problem "![](images/77/776ef945cb188befda6d6479bf10120428e9b77efcd4634c9bec02ecf4134cfc.png)\n\nWhich of the following gives the graph of the straight line above?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's pick two distinct points on the line. For example, $A$ and $B$ with coordinates $(0,1)$ and $(3,-1)$, respectively.\n\n![](images/2f/2f534e895418435f613e47853d84c692fce0281cd1f11bfe4779c84d33712f46.png)\n\nNow, we substitute the coordinates of both points in our equations. If both points satisfy an equation, then we can conclude that the equation represents the line in the graph. Otherwise, if any point does *not* satisfy the equation, then we can conclude that the equation does *not* represent the line in the graph.\n\n- Equation: $y=\\frac{2}{3}x+1.$\nSubstituting the coordinates of $A(0,1)$ and $B(3,-1)$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(1) &=\\frac{2}{3}(0)+1 \\\\ 1 &=1\\,\\checkmark \\\\ (-1) &=\\frac{2}{3}(3)+1 \\\\ -1 &=3\\,\\times\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $y=\\frac{2}{3}x+1$ is *not* an equation of the line in the graph.\n\n- Equation: $2y-\\frac{4}{3}x=2.$\nSubstituting the coordinates of $A(0,1)$ and $B(3,-1)$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(1)-\\frac{4}{3}(0) &=2 \\\\ 2 &=2\\,\\checkmark \\\\ 2(-1)-\\frac{4}{3}(3) &=2 \\\\ -6 &=2\\,\\times\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $2y-\\frac{4}{3}x=2$ is *not* an equation of the line in the graph.\n\n- Equation: $y=1-\\frac{2}{3}x.$\nSubstituting the coordinates of $A(0,1)$ and $B(3,-1)$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(1) &=1-\\frac{2}{3}(0) \\\\ 1 &=1\\,\\checkmark \\\\ (-1) &=1-\\frac{2}{3}(3) \\\\ -1 &=-1\\,\\checkmark\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $y=1-\\frac{2}{3}x$ is an equation of the line in the graph.\n\nSelect $y=1-\\frac{2}{3}x$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186624848 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aef1b9ae-7126-56d5-baa9-b20f87a08cdf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624826} {:answer/id #uuid "e2dd2fe2-9987-549f-9d23-fc35b34b236f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624842}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e2dd2fe2-9987-549f-9d23-fc35b34b236f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624842} :answer-field/id #uuid "8263c959-51f7-5d3d-8c43-be6ccd1df0a0" :answer-field/key "$y=-1+\\frac{3}{2}x$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624822} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "47a631e9-9670-5c0c-ac57-4ae3fb775d3e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624811} {:answer/id #uuid "47d399b6-ac89-5a80-b0bb-554849d5c25d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624812}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "47d399b6-ac89-5a80-b0bb-554849d5c25d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624812} :answer-field/id #uuid "c381b027-e8e4-50a0-9be8-62cb031c1c16" :answer-field/key "$2y-3x=-2$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624832} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6c18d31a-cc19-57b2-90c7-f599c0c66e6c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624818} {:answer/id #uuid "caea7151-5d36-5bb5-874b-89fb58d5369b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624834}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "caea7151-5d36-5bb5-874b-89fb58d5369b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624834} :answer-field/id #uuid "dcb96b7b-7963-5616-9a2f-9a347bf062fe" :answer-field/key "$y=\\frac{2}{3}x-1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624840}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f282ccdc-a340-5563-90cb-3edb0578b2ab" :question/problem "![](images/a4/a49ee497281145f15b2ba053557e1f783ec98f9cd41f83a8d77ec3ddf8c60813.png)\n\nWhich of the following gives the graph of the straight line above?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's pick two distinct points on the line. For example, $A$ and $B$ with coordinates $(0,-1)$ and $(2,2)$, respectively.\n\n![](images/11/11926789df1b1240bb41a88bddc7fea03f81e1f23f813add7de979b3afe777fa.png)\n\nNow, we substitute the coordinates of both points in our equations. If both points satisfy an equation, then we can conclude that the equation represents the line in the graph. Otherwise, if any point does *not* satisfy the equation, then we can conclude that the equation does *not* represent the line in the graph.\n\n- Equation: $y=\\frac{2}{3}x-1.$\nSubstituting the coordinates of $A(0,-1)$ and $B(2,2)$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-1) &=\\frac{2}{3}(0)-1 \\\\ -1 &=-1\\,\\checkmark \\\\ (2) &=\\frac{2}{3}(2)-1 \\\\ 2 &=\\frac{1}{3}\\,\\times\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $y=\\frac{2}{3}x-1$ is *not* an equation of the line in the graph.\n\n- Equation: $2y-3x=-2.$\nSubstituting the coordinates of $A(0,-1)$ and $B(2,2)$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(-1)-3(0) &=-2 \\\\ -2 &=-2\\,\\checkmark \\\\ 2(2)-3(2) &=-2 \\\\ -2 &=-2\\,\\checkmark\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $2y-3x=-2$ is an equation of the line in the graph.\n\n- Equation: $y=-1+\\frac{3}{2}x.$\nSubstituting the coordinates of $A(0,-1)$ and $B(2,2)$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-1) &=-1+\\frac{3}{2}(0) \\\\ -1 &=-1\\,\\checkmark \\\\ (2) &=-1+\\frac{3}{2}(2) \\\\ 2 &=2\\,\\checkmark\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $y=-1+\\frac{3}{2}x$ is an equation of the line in the graph.\n\nSelect $2y-3x=-2$, $y=-1+\\frac{3}{2}x$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186624849 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "70b98ffb-80cb-5ca4-bd4c-259be4760585" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624819} {:answer/id #uuid "d3750699-e025-55fe-a799-cf86276cb98d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624836}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "70b98ffb-80cb-5ca4-bd4c-259be4760585" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624819} :answer-field/id #uuid "80bc88b4-25c2-5f15-9746-21faf2ee8e90" :answer-field/key "$y+\\frac{2}{3}x=-3$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624821} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "518a4bdb-8dcd-5207-b502-4aafcf9a9acd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624813} {:answer/id #uuid "e719501a-040e-5570-af42-99c67304a516" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624844}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "518a4bdb-8dcd-5207-b502-4aafcf9a9acd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624813} :answer-field/id #uuid "c531402c-f61a-5f5d-9748-d54b2a954344" :answer-field/key "$y=- \\frac{3}{2}x-3$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624833} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b1e069e5-16e7-52c3-97c9-97869e2457a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624827} {:answer/id #uuid "b4c149a1-4dac-5c62-bb14-a83c5383c8bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624829}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b1e069e5-16e7-52c3-97c9-97869e2457a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624827} :answer-field/id #uuid "e8c159f9-9229-5bd8-91dc-863dea7f745b" :answer-field/key "$y=-3-\\frac{2}{3}x$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624846}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f8ed05a3-a2f1-5d93-9961-f5cdb8afd0d8" :question/problem "![](images/58/58fe55d2d673fb6ad2335444e6b704a7139b591304ee4fa883bfd37adb295661.png)\n\nWhich of the following gives the graph of the straight line above?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's pick two distinct points on the line. For example, $A$ and $B$ with coordinates $(0,-3)$ and $(2,-6)$, respectively.\n\n![](images/75/75097de1c2a2d54e75ddbc626f01da74ad6fd21bc6d1d57eb5bc4b06a6fd8bcc.png)\n\nNow, we substitute the coordinates of both points in our equations. If both points satisfy an equation, then we can conclude that the equation represents the line in the graph. Otherwise, if any point does *not* satisfy the equation, then we can conclude that the equation does *not* represent the line in the graph.\n\n- Equation: $y=- \\frac{3}{2}x-3.$\nSubstituting the coordinates of $A(0,-3)$ and $B(2,-6)$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-3) &=- \\frac{3}{2}(0)-3 \\\\ -3 &=-3\\,\\checkmark \\\\ (-6) &=- \\frac{3}{2}(2)-3 \\\\ -6 &=-6\\,\\checkmark\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $y=- \\frac{3}{2}x-3$ is an equation of the line in the graph.\n\n- Equation: $y=-3-\\frac{2}{3}x.$\nSubstituting the coordinates of $A(0,-3)$ and $B(2,-6)$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-3) &=-3-\\frac{2}{3}(0) \\\\ -3 &=-3\\,\\checkmark \\\\ (-6) &=-3-\\frac{2}{3}(2) \\\\ -6 &=- \\frac{13}{3}\\,\\times\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $y=-3-\\frac{2}{3}x$ is *not* an equation of the line in the graph.\n\n- Equation: $y+\\frac{2}{3}x=-3.$\nSubstituting the coordinates of $A(0,-3)$ and $B(2,-6)$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-3)+\\frac{2}{3}(0) &=-3 \\\\ -3 &=-3\\,\\checkmark \\\\ (-6)+\\frac{2}{3}(2) &=-3 \\\\ - \\frac{14}{3} &=-3\\,\\times\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $y+\\frac{2}{3}x=-3$ is *not* an equation of the line in the graph.\n\nSelect $y=- \\frac{3}{2}x-3$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186631884 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "53da5106-e70d-5ad1-967f-be43ef65a87e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{x}^{2}+y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186631359} {:answer/id #uuid "7641aae1-5cea-5e62-bc13-f69281245d5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}^{2}-\\sqrt{2}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186631428} {:answer/id #uuid "d18778e9-051b-5a37-9f69-e60c5f460fa7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-x-2{y}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186631627} {:answer/id #uuid "d5125629-e1a8-53f9-90e9-35ff079d06bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{x}^{2}-2y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186631635} {:answer/id #uuid "d8e2477e-c358-5333-a3dd-60457a919cfb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2{x}^{2}-y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186631646}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d8e2477e-c358-5333-a3dd-60457a919cfb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2{x}^{2}-y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186631646} :answer-field/id #uuid "48b618e3-2e1d-5898-8dd7-356068fbebc0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186631768}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "557300de-09b3-5e0a-8a2f-375395204316" :question/math-academy-id "q-69652" :question/problem "Calculate $det(M)$, if\n $$\n\\displaystyle M=\\begin{bmatrix}2x & \\sqrt{y} \\\\ \\sqrt{y} & -x\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{vmatrix}=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(M) & =\\begin{vmatrix}2x & \\sqrt{y} \\\\ \\sqrt{y} & -x\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2x\\cdot (-x)-\\sqrt{y}\\cdot \\sqrt{y} \\\\  & =-2{x}^{2}-y\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186632064 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "267a0355-2f9b-591a-a5b7-f3122f078c98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{8}}{8}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632068} {:answer/id #uuid "284fdc57-cace-5ff2-b2e8-df45d06148e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{7}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632069} {:answer/id #uuid "2e73719e-1858-5ad9-b105-75906d9dc2a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{7}}{7}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632070} {:answer/id #uuid "96e019a9-8f39-5b51-b043-48a8a145a7c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{7}}{8}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632081} {:answer/id #uuid "bbfadeb9-5cb3-5120-b16c-a60acc2bbc47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{8}}{7}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632087}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "267a0355-2f9b-591a-a5b7-f3122f078c98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{8}}{8}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632068} :answer-field/id #uuid "7f051dfe-f49c-5b19-bcaf-65f74a79dd8b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632078}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "21d74d11-27ac-56bf-bae4-d75f49dbc257" :question/problem "Calculate $F(x)$ given that $f(x)={x}^{7}$ and ${F}^{'}(x)=f(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that integration is the opposite of differentiation. So, if ${F}^{'}(x)=f(x),$ then integrating both sides of this equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{F}^{'}(x) & =f(x) \\\\ \\int {F}^{'}(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ F(x) & =\\int f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe apply the power rule with $n=7$, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x) & =\\int f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {x}^{7}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{7+1}}{7+1}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{8}}{8}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's check by differentiating:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{x}^{8}}{8}+C) &= \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\left(\\frac{{x}^{8}}{8}\\right)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\ &= \\frac{1}{8}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{8})+0 \\\\ &= \\frac{1}{8}\\cdot 8\\,{x}^{7} \\\\ &= {x}^{7}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186632066 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "22bcf2a9-77c7-5d82-b345-bdbb1e3f1ab9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{13}}{13}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632065} {:answer/id #uuid "305fca67-8c31-5139-bcad-b9fcdc295fe3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{13}}{12}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632071} {:answer/id #uuid "71071747-9658-5ec2-8413-923f0d38d0e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{12}}{13}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632077} {:answer/id #uuid "b086dc51-77e7-5eb2-891d-94c25c362f6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{12}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632086} {:answer/id #uuid "f146687b-9d31-527b-a2b2-004105d155ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{12}}{12}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632093}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "22bcf2a9-77c7-5d82-b345-bdbb1e3f1ab9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{13}}{13}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632065} :answer-field/id #uuid "687d9602-d083-5dde-849c-37c5281d7a0c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632076}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2400a578-4e3e-50d6-aaa1-b71cd0eb4bcd" :question/problem "Calculate $$\n\\displaystyle \\int {x}^{12}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We apply the power rule with $n=12$, and we get\n\n$$\n\\int {x}^{12}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{{x}^{12+1}}{12+1}+C=\\frac{{x}^{13}}{13}+C.\n$$\n\nLet's check by differentiating:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{x}^{13}}{13}+C) &= \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\left(\\frac{{x}^{13}}{13}\\right)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\ &= \\frac{1}{13}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{13})+0 \\\\ &= \\frac{1}{13}\\cdot 13{x}^{12} \\\\ &= {x}^{12}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186632067 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "431270bd-146d-5112-b887-738a04648b51" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{7}}{7}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632074} {:answer/id #uuid "851a58e8-4f4d-5e1e-baec-320b49fd6198" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{7}}{6}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632079} {:answer/id #uuid "af29b014-c606-5fe0-a9dc-c8b52250806b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{6}}{6}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632085} {:answer/id #uuid "cf96ecc9-b2ab-5851-b199-ec857eeed39e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{7}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632089} {:answer/id #uuid "e47afe31-bd30-5b7b-8e1a-8407781f6103" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{6}}{7}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632092}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "af29b014-c606-5fe0-a9dc-c8b52250806b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{6}}{6}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632085} :answer-field/id #uuid "f160be36-0205-577c-a3ce-ed30257270ff" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632094}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "24a65f7f-6166-52b0-b66b-e7bb9af593bd" :question/problem "Calculate $F(x)$ given that $f(x)={x}^{5}$ and ${F}^{'}(x)=f(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that integration is the opposite of differentiation. So, if ${F}^{'}(x)=f(x),$ then integrating both sides of this equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{F}^{'}(x) & =f(x) \\\\ \\int {F}^{'}(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ F(x) & =\\int f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe apply the power rule with $n=5$, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x) & =\\int f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {x}^{5}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{5+1}}{5+1}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{6}}{6}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's check by differentiating:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{x}^{6}}{6}+C) &= \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\left(\\frac{{x}^{6}}{6}\\right)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\ &= \\frac{1}{6}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{6})+0 \\\\ &= \\frac{1}{6}\\cdot 6\\,{x}^{5} \\\\ &= {x}^{5}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186632088 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09aece13-93fe-51d3-8a5d-b4a2ab7eb067" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{21}}{20}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632063} {:answer/id #uuid "98f7e536-8b26-5303-9dc1-3a28e6569a4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{20}}{21}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632082} {:answer/id #uuid "a280dfca-6b2b-56aa-9b48-fcaa1280329f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{20}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632083} {:answer/id #uuid "a4d0b5e0-9440-5979-a5ee-fc2cca5875bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{21}}{21}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632084} {:answer/id #uuid "f68f88e0-cb47-5014-b256-da46f2b718bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{20}}{20}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632096}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f68f88e0-cb47-5014-b256-da46f2b718bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{20}}{20}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632096} :answer-field/id #uuid "da6746a6-59ee-52ba-93e6-d5310d5500c0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632090}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "bd7041ea-d08b-5844-9b3c-40be8cd0bd12" :question/problem "Calculate $F(x)$ given that $f(x)={x}^{19}$ and ${F}^{'}(x)=f(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that integration is the opposite of differentiation. So, if ${F}^{'}(x)=f(x),$ then integrating both sides of this equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{F}^{'}(x) & =f(x) \\\\ \\int {F}^{'}(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ F(x) & =\\int f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe apply the power rule with $n=19$, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x) & =\\int f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {x}^{19}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{19+1}}{19+1}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{20}}{20}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's check by differentiating:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{x}^{20}}{20}+C) &= \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\left(\\frac{{x}^{20}}{20}\\right)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\ &= \\frac{1}{20}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{20})+0 \\\\ &= \\frac{1}{20}\\cdot 20\\,{x}^{19} \\\\ &= {x}^{19}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186632091 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05e4247c-6054-5f84-84f5-ed5f824d5d90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{5}}{5}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632062} {:answer/id #uuid "3bf81e1c-d2d5-5a7d-9e79-6d2e3e314f3e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{4}}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632072} {:answer/id #uuid "66cf396e-3228-5244-9f4c-aedcae1d70c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{5}}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632075} {:answer/id #uuid "8783c8dd-e5fa-5f7a-af8f-c4b7a7c68b03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{5}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632080} {:answer/id #uuid "f545b0d2-fda1-55ef-b61e-183b5bad59a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{4}}{5}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632095}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "05e4247c-6054-5f84-84f5-ed5f824d5d90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{5}}{5}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632062} :answer-field/id #uuid "3cc5e987-43f3-52ec-8e2d-dacca1c43b26" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632073}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e44b04a5-8d3e-56fa-ae3e-15c4f664b2e9" :question/problem "Calculate $$\n\\displaystyle \\int {x}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We apply the power rule with $n=4$, and we get\n\n$$\n\\int {x}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{{x}^{4+1}}{4+1}+C=\\frac{{x}^{5}}{5}+C.\n$$\n\nLet's check by differentiating:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{x}^{5}}{5}+C) &= \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\left(\\frac{{x}^{5}}{5}\\right)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\ &= \\frac{1}{5}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{5})+0 \\\\ &= \\frac{1}{5}\\cdot 5{x}^{4} \\\\ &= {x}^{4}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186632107 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "383c9cf4-9999-544c-9991-3e389d1e8202" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{13/4}}{6} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632105} {:answer/id #uuid "ab127b7a-c644-50b9-bc45-4f314b20034a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4{x}^{13/4}}{7} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632115} {:answer/id #uuid "ae4352af-5818-5677-9495-de1a6e17db7a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4{x}^{7/4}}{11} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632116} {:answer/id #uuid "b947531c-3eee-5e80-84c9-04e32ec0a073" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{7/4}}{6} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632118} {:answer/id #uuid "d907ffd1-f01c-539b-a1de-9df33d4a67e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4{x}^{7/4}}{7} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632122}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d907ffd1-f01c-539b-a1de-9df33d4a67e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4{x}^{7/4}}{7} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632122} :answer-field/id #uuid "3c2dc46f-f898-5487-b33d-e094e125e98f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632106}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "477b81fd-0d41-5aeb-9d0d-bfba79f45ad8" :question/problem "Find the antiderivative of ${x}^{3/4}.$\n\nWork on $x>0$." :question/worked-solution "We can apply the power rule with $n=\\frac{3}{4}$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {x}^{3/4}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{{x}^{3/4+1}}{(\\frac{3}{4}+1)}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{7/4}}{\\left(\\frac{7}{4}\\right)}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{4{x}^{7/4}}{7}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAgain, let's check by differentiating:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{4{x}^{7/4}}{7}+C) &= \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\left(\\frac{4{x}^{7/4}}{7}\\right)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\ &= \\frac{4}{7}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{7/4})+0 \\\\ &= \\frac{4}{7}\\cdot \\frac{7}{4}{x}^{7/4-1} \\\\ &= {x}^{3/4}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186632110 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02f8b77e-17f1-5387-a87d-23a3ff99934a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5{x}^{1/3} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632098} {:answer/id #uuid "12bd4168-b5bc-5325-b188-fea546b91b46" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5{x}^{4/3} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632099} {:answer/id #uuid "32e4276b-e685-51a3-8475-846db1f81282" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3{x}^{1/3}}{4} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632103} {:answer/id #uuid "c83531c0-b308-538b-9