eld/correct {:answer/id #uuid "70bf4863-92e7-5e95-9fd6-c2a589917968" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4{x}^{9/4}}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632109} :answer-field/id #uuid "b84da965-e3fc-5ba0-9917-0cb5af5d27bc" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632117}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9b882599-473b-551d-be43-1f32e525912f" :question/problem "Find the antiderivative of ${x}^{5/4}.$\n\nWork on $x>0$.\n\nThe antiderivative is {{field-1}} $+C$. Enter only the term before $+C$, with no additive constant." :question/worked-solution "We can apply the power rule with $n=\\frac{5}{4}$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {x}^{5/4}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{{x}^{5/4+1}}{(\\frac{5}{4}+1)}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{9/4}}{\\left(\\frac{9}{4}\\right)}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{4{x}^{9/4}}{9}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAgain, let's check by differentiating:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{4{x}^{9/4}}{9}+C) &= \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\left(\\frac{4{x}^{9/4}}{9}\\right)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\ &= \\frac{4}{9}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{9/4})+0 \\\\ &= \\frac{4}{9}\\cdot \\frac{9}{4}{x}^{9/4-1} \\\\ &= {x}^{5/4}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186632114 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ec493b07-43f5-5006-bf2b-4faff02253cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3{x}^{4/3}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632124}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ec493b07-43f5-5006-bf2b-4faff02253cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3{x}^{4/3}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632124} :answer-field/id #uuid "78fa16cd-fb2e-5d4f-8ed2-80a699116f20" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632111}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a48b925b-78c0-5a09-affb-691438624f03" :question/problem "The antiderivative of $\\sqrt[3]{x}$ equals {{field-1}} $+C$.\n\nWork on $x>0$. Enter only the term before $+C$, with no additive constant." :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "Since $\\sqrt[3]{x}={x}^{1/3}$, we can apply the power rule with $n=\\frac{1}{3}$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {x}^{1/3}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{{x}^{1/3+1}}{(\\frac{1}{3}+1)}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{4/3}}{\\left(\\frac{4}{3}\\right)}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{3{x}^{4/3}}{4}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's check our answer by differentiating:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{3{x}^{4/3}}{4}+C) &= \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\left(\\frac{3{x}^{4/3}}{4}\\right)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\ &= \\frac{3}{4}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{4/3})+0 \\\\ &= \\frac{3}{4}\\cdot \\frac{4}{3}{x}^{4/3-1} \\\\ &= {x}^{1/3}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186632119 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "165347ea-8cc0-5126-bbd5-7fa6bd55f039" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4{x}^{1}}{5} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632100} {:answer/id #uuid "236f3c6d-6e65-5105-a485-32f39b7fe38b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7{x}^{5/4}}{8} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632101} {:answer/id #uuid "249e2652-bbbb-5e2a-add1-2527b04b268e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4{x}^{5/4}}{5} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632102} {:answer/id #uuid "a213afe2-4e5b-56cc-9508-969c8ab27731" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5{x}^{1}}{9} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632113} {:answer/id #uuid "e6e3cc44-b079-532e-b82f-181f8049ee49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7{x}^{1}}{8} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632123}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "249e2652-bbbb-5e2a-add1-2527b04b268e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4{x}^{5/4}}{5} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632102} :answer-field/id #uuid "3336ec14-fc88-58c0-bf1e-5c78ea812139" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632104}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "be181925-3dc1-585c-8a3a-66f07078c674" :question/problem "Find the antiderivative of ${x}^{1/4}.$\n\nWork on $x>0$." :question/worked-solution "We can apply the power rule with $n=\\frac{1}{4}$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {x}^{1/4}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{{x}^{1/4+1}}{(\\frac{1}{4}+1)}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{5/4}}{\\left(\\frac{5}{4}\\right)}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{4{x}^{5/4}}{5}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAgain, let's check by differentiating:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{4{x}^{5/4}}{5}+C) &= \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\left(\\frac{4{x}^{5/4}}{5}\\right)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\ &= \\frac{4}{5}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{5/4})+0 \\\\ &= \\frac{4}{5}\\cdot \\frac{5}{4}{x}^{5/4-1} \\\\ &= {x}^{1/4}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186632685 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "24e4bb45-d508-5b70-8ed2-f20eeac35ac7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3-\\sqrt{2}z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632180} {:answer/id #uuid "43a035f5-e17f-596a-ae9d-b69bc4af5b9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2+3z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632233} {:answer/id #uuid "469b0701-86d6-5c2f-b831-b0922d1f108a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}-3z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632243} {:answer/id #uuid "6a1394b3-db21-57d8-8761-69658e219f6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}+3z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632304} {:answer/id #uuid "d7fea6f7-ac67-5882-b9b2-ba8e1ad1c432" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2-3z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632473}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d7fea6f7-ac67-5882-b9b2-ba8e1ad1c432" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2-3z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632473} :answer-field/id #uuid "8b8c93d5-4aa0-5aa8-8854-3c4446fcbfee" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632607}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5c832111-7e26-5f06-bbf5-0fe500587e8b" :question/math-academy-id "q-69648" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle \\begin{vmatrix}\\sqrt{2} & z \\\\ 3 & \\sqrt{2}\\end{vmatrix}=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{vmatrix}=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{vmatrix}\\sqrt{2} & 3 \\\\ z & \\sqrt{2}\\end{vmatrix} & =\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{2}-z\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =2-3z\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186632688 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a492949-3bd3-5139-a09e-bd9913dab194" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632169} {:answer/id #uuid "60936ee6-077a-5769-8dc2-3c8fefce1f0d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632286} {:answer/id #uuid "8ef20736-29c1-50f0-84a6-1558444988de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632364} {:answer/id #uuid "ca1c6019-99d5-5cac-a1f8-9077432f3728" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632446} {:answer/id #uuid "f70a2a78-ceac-54fe-b05a-31a8e59bf980" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632529}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ca1c6019-99d5-5cac-a1f8-9077432f3728" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632446} :answer-field/id #uuid "10a75dfb-dbb7-5551-954d-06078da5405d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632550}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "67bf1af6-08b7-5d3a-b028-0c31c332e000" :question/math-academy-id "q-11647" :question/problem "If\n$$\n\\displaystyle B=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & x \\\\ 2 & 6\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\nand\n$\\text{det}(B)=2$, what is the value of $x?$" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{vmatrix}=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(B) & =\\begin{vmatrix}2 & x \\\\ 2 & 6\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 6-x\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =12-2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince $det(B)=2$, we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B) & =2 \\\\ 12-2x & =2 \\\\ -2x & =2-12 \\\\ -2x & =-10 \\\\ x & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186632702 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "37d076a4-6367-5487-9f22-ea5c34784e3a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632215}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "37d076a4-6367-5487-9f22-ea5c34784e3a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632215} :answer-field/id #uuid "c2f8f65c-9492-5e44-a731-352186ac01a7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632623}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "948a413c-4dce-57f7-8b58-de4a73761168" :question/math-academy-id "q-275599" :question/problem "If\n$$\n\\displaystyle A=\\begin{bmatrix}3+t & 4t \\\\ -3 & 3-t\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\nand $det(A)=45,$ what is the value of $t?$\n\n$t=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{vmatrix}=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =\\begin{vmatrix}3+t & 4t \\\\ -3 & 3-t\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(3+t)(3-t)-4t(-3) \\\\  & =9-{t}^{2}+12t \\\\  & =-{t}^{2}+12t+9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(A)=45$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =45 \\\\ -{t}^{2}+12t+9 & =45 \\\\ -{t}^{2}+12t-36 & =0 \\\\ {t}^{2}-12t+36 & =0 \\\\ (t-6)^{2} & =0 \\\\ t & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186632818 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ffcc9c8-fa08-54c7-b2ad-c534fcf250d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{{x}^{1/2}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632817} {:answer/id #uuid "25e9b4fa-b3b8-53b4-a463-ae5fa9f91f81" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{{x}^{9/2}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632819} {:answer/id #uuid "3d392c6d-b3a0-55f0-8421-991ed1909ed7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{5{x}^{1/2}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632822} {:answer/id #uuid "87eb4ecf-01c3-53b6-b85a-7cf25ee8a9ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{5{x}^{5/2}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632837} {:answer/id #uuid "ae0a00ea-ab15-53bf-bbe0-f78f449ce528" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{{x}^{5/2}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632842}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "87eb4ecf-01c3-53b6-b85a-7cf25ee8a9ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{5{x}^{5/2}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632837} :answer-field/id #uuid "3e4e29b3-1d79-581b-90fd-f6060e9ce8de" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632823}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2413cfbc-6c20-5a51-891c-672965174302" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)=\\frac{1}{{x}^{7/2}}$ and that ${F}^{'}(x)=f(x)$, calculate $F(x).$ Assume $x>0$." :question/worked-solution "Remember that integration is the opposite of differentiation. So, if ${F}^{'}(x)=f(x),$ then integrating both sides of this equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{F}^{'}(x) & =f(x) \\\\ \\int {F}^{'}(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ F(x) & =\\int f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $\\frac{1}{{x}^{7/2}}={x}^{-7/2}.$ So, we can use the power rule with $n=-\\frac{7}{2}$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x) & =\\int f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {x}^{-7/2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{-7/2+1}}{(-\\frac{7}{2}+1)}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{-5/2}}{\\left(-\\frac{5}{2}\\right)}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{5}{x}^{-5/2}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{5{x}^{5/2}}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186632820 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "40977a8b-4863-516a-972a-3a34abc21243" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{7}{x}^{-3/2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632825} {:answer/id #uuid "40d3b3cb-8e93-5649-94ea-6e727dc46fa1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{-7/2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632826} {:answer/id #uuid "508d6e9f-a218-51a5-85a7-9a0e43544f7e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{7}{x}^{-7/6}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632828} {:answer/id #uuid "587e46be-90b5-568f-97f7-aeea7f29cf0f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{7}{x}^{-7/2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632829} {:answer/id #uuid "abad993c-1355-59f7-9f27-49c83c474eb2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{-3/2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632841}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "587e46be-90b5-568f-97f7-aeea7f29cf0f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{7}{x}^{-7/2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632829} :answer-field/id #uuid "5a425b0e-b155-5ef4-a994-32f805dfde0d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632831}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2e7a9040-6cde-56d7-a463-866319328df1" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{9}}}$ and that ${F}^{'}(x)=f(x)$, calculate $F(x).$ Assume $x>0$." :question/worked-solution "Remember that integration is the opposite of differentiation. So, if ${F}^{'}(x)=f(x),$ then integrating both sides of this equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{F}^{'}(x) & =f(x) \\\\ \\int {F}^{'}(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ F(x) & =\\int f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{9}}}={x}^{-9/2}.$ So, we can use the power rule with $n=-\\frac{9}{2}$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x) & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{9}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {x}^{-9/2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{-9/2+1}}{(-\\frac{9}{2}+1)}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{-7/2}}{\\left(-\\frac{7}{2}\\right)}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{7}{x}^{-7/2}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186632821 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03459bdb-f82c-52d3-a1be-9cf84949b9bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2{x}^{-1/2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632815} {:answer/id #uuid "7e485733-affe-5550-b0b1-0008e5746e83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{7}{x}^{-3/2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632836} {:answer/id #uuid "c0c513de-d62a-5f43-87fa-6497586e1b5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{7}{x}^{-7/2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632843} {:answer/id #uuid "f4f21317-af0a-58eb-b862-a55e79d4e17b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{7}{x}^{-1/2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632848} {:answer/id #uuid "fa796935-5678-55f3-8b41-1a98f5730810" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2{x}^{-3/2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632849}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c0c513de-d62a-5f43-87fa-6497586e1b5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{7}{x}^{-7/2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632843} :answer-field/id #uuid "a22107ac-398a-5313-be3a-7841e8a9ef3f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632839}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "34f8e342-2cc0-5379-827c-e6ea111173a7" :question/problem "Calculate the integral of $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{9}}}$. Assume $x>0$." :question/worked-solution "Note that $$\n\\displaystyle \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{9}}}=\\frac{1}{{x}^{9/2}}={x}^{-9/2}.\n$$ So, we can use the power rule with $n=-\\frac{9}{2}$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{9}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {x}^{-9/2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{-9/2+1}}{-\\frac{9}{2}+1}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{7}{x}^{-7/2}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{7{x}^{7/2}}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186632827 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e5ff9a9-8634-55ed-8d18-9bf7b3b3068e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{5{x}^{3/4}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632824} {:answer/id #uuid "7dfcfb5c-b9a8-5b12-b428-01cd27f22d5f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{5{x}^{9/4}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632835} {:answer/id #uuid "91381b87-bac0-57a5-8ad2-3f9990f1c77c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{3{x}^{9/4}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632838} {:answer/id #uuid "a51ccdc2-c823-5b46-8fb2-7ea81da8261c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{5{x}^{5/3}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632840} {:answer/id #uuid "c5e76ee5-682e-55c7-a0a6-5a52b10e50a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{3{x}^{3/4}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632844}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a51ccdc2-c823-5b46-8fb2-7ea81da8261c" 